{
  "version": "0.1.0",
  "notes": [
    "Layer 2 (structure) rules. content/structure.js measures the page — what is floating over it, how its buttons are styled, which boxes are ticked — and lib/structural.js judges those measurements against the vocabulary and thresholds below.",
    "Like Layer 1, every rule maps to one of the five Gray et al. (2024) strategies so the popup can group results consistently.",
    "A pop-up only counts as an interruption if it opened without a click or key press just before it. Something the shopper opened themselves is not nagging.",
    "Cookie and consent banners are never reported as interruptions — they are legally required — but their buttons are still measured for bias. Once a consent choice has been measured, the Layer 1 rules listed in 'settles' are dropped for that page: the measurement replaces the wording-based guess, whichever way it comes out.",
    "A cancel or unsubscribe link counts as hidden when its text is under hiddenLinkFontPx pixels or below hiddenLinkContrast against its background — the same 3:1 line WCAG draws for large text, so normal grey footer links (about 4.5:1) are not flagged.",
    "Button prominence uses WCAG 2 contrast ratios, so faintContrast 3.0 is the same line accessibility guidance draws for large text.",
    "Vocabulary entries are case-insensitive regular expressions, matched against button labels, checkbox labels or pop-up text after curly apostrophes are straightened."
  ],
  "thresholds": {
    "barMinWidth": 0.9,
    "barMaxHeight": 0.25,
    "smallMaxCoverage": 0.12,
    "dialogMinCoverage": 0.25,
    "minContentChars": 8,
    "visibleFillContrast": 1.05,
    "strongFillChroma": 0.25,
    "strongFillContrast": 3.0,
    "outlineContrast": 1.5,
    "sizeRatio": 0.5,
    "fontRatio": 0.8,
    "faintContrast": 3.0,
    "biasThreshold": 1.5,
    "hiddenLinkContrast": 3.0,
    "hiddenLinkFontPx": 10.5
  },
  "vocabulary": {
